#version 450
// vt::RmsNorm — the WIDE variant. Same body, same math, same numerics tier as
// vt_rms_norm.comp (both include vt_rms_norm_body.glsl); the ONLY differences are
// the workgroup width and the reduction shape:
//
//   * VT_TG 1024 instead of 128, and a matching `local_size_x` literal;
//   * VT_SUBGROUP_REDUCE, so vt_tg_sum collapses each subgroup with subgroupAdd
//     and takes ONE barrier instead of log2(VT_TG) of them.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS — MEASURED, not assumed (VK-RMSNORM, GB10, 2026-08-09).
// vt::RmsNorm dispatches ONE WORKGROUP PER ROW, and a batch-1 decode step has
// exactly one row: the host launches `groups = t = 1`. On Qwen3.6-27B that is a
// single 128-invocation workgroup walking h = 5120 elements, i.e. 40 loop
// iterations on 4 warps of ONE streaming multiprocessor while the rest of the GPU
// idles. The instrument that showed it is the two-length GPU-timestamp diff
// (output-len 36 minus output-len 4, so prefill and one-time costs cancel):
// vt_rms_norm cost 0.0611 ms/call and 7.88 ms/token across 129 calls/token, about
// TEN TIMES the other small kernels, while reading only ~20 KB — far under a
// microsecond at the 273 GB/s roof. The decisive attribution is that the SAME
// shader in the SAME run costs 0.0667 ms/call during PREFILL, where it is handed
// 32 rows and therefore 32 workgroups and 32x the data: 32x the work for 9% more
// time is not a kernel doing work, it is a kernel waiting, and the idle machine
// is the lever. `vt_rms_norm_gated`, which reduces identically but is launched
// with 48 workgroups, costs 0.0055 ms/call — the reduction was never the
// difference, the OCCUPANCY was.
//
// llama.cpp reaches the same conclusion by two other routes at the same pin
// (237ad9b96): its `rms_norm.comp:33` runs BLOCK_SIZE 512 rather than the
// guaranteed-portable 128, and `rms_norm_partials.comp` exists solely to spread a
// SINGLE row across many workgroups when the row count cannot. Widening the
// workgroup is the half of that which needs no second dispatch and no
// cross-workgroup hand-off, so it is what this module does.
//
// NOT PORTABLE, WHICH IS WHY IT IS A SEPARATE MODULE. 1024 invocations exceed the
// Vulkan-guaranteed minimum of 128, and the subgroup instructions need
// capabilities a conformant device may lack. The host probes
// maxComputeWorkGroupInvocations, maxComputeWorkGroupSize.x and
// VkPhysicalDeviceSubgroupProperties and falls back to vt_rms_norm.comp when any
// of them is missing (src/vt/vulkan/vulkan_ops.cpp § RmsNormKernel).
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require

#define VT_TG 1024u
#define VT_SUBGROUP_REDUCE

layout(local_size_x = 1024, local_size_y = 1, local_size_z = 1) in;

#include "vt_rms_norm_body.glsl"
